q: {about to yank a usb drive -- flush everything buffered out to disk|force every dirty buffer out to disk right now|write all pending buffered data to disk}
a: sync
why: root
ref: sync
teach: sync
hint: sync with no arguments flushes every dirty buffer on the system
---
q: {you just wrote @txt@, don't risk losing it -- flush only its data|flush just @txt@'s buffered data, leaving the rest alone|write out only @txt@'s pending data, not every buffer}
a: sync -d @txt@
why: root
ref: sync
teach: sync -d
hint: -d limits the flush to the file you name
---
q: {hold an exclusive lock on lock.file so two copies never overlap|hold an exclusive lock on lock.file while a command runs|use lock.file as an exclusive lock around a command}
a: flock -x lock.file echo held
out: held
ref: flock
teach: flock -x
hint: -x is flock's default, an exclusive lock -- named here for clarity
---
q: {take the lock but give up immediately if someone else holds it|try the lock and bail out at once if it is already held|attempt lock.file's lock, failing instantly rather than waiting}
a: flock -n lock.file echo held
out: held
ref: flock
teach: flock -n
hint: -n makes flock fail instead of waiting when the lock is held
---
q: {take a shared lock rather than an exclusive one|take lock.file's lock as shared, not exclusive|hold a shared lock instead of an exclusive one}
a: flock -s lock.file echo held
out: held
ref: flock
teach: flock -s
hint: -s takes a shared lock, which can coexist with other shared locks
